<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_4_6" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_4_6" name="4.6 Restore the work site" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>All six processes are drawn. This group came into the model later than the rest of 4.0, from the 2026 read of the programme documents, and it is graded P/1 rather than P/2 because one programme documented it as a contracted two-stage programme.

THE PERMIT CLOCK IS THE SPINE, and it is why 4.6.6 exists as a process rather than as a status field. A temporary reinstatement is lawful for a period the jurisdiction sets, and the obligation to make it permanent survives the work order, the crew and often the contractor. 2.6.4 owns the permit cost, expiry and renewal; this group tracks the restoration against it and escalates BEFORE breach rather than reporting after.

Two stages, not one act, and the gap between them is the process. 4.6.2 inspects and repairs the temporary condition for as long as it stands, because a temporary reinstatement that degrades is a public hazard and a claim - and it is the step that quietly does not happen when a permanent-restoration backlog builds.

MUTCD is cited at 4.6.4 for traffic and public protection. It is public law and it is one of the few places in this category where a control has a regulation behind it rather than practice.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_4_6_lanes">
      <lane id="l_46_field" name="Field and restoration crew">
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_ass</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_tmp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_t</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_insp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_acc</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_fix</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_perm</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_evid</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_corr</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_46_obl" name="Permit and obligation owner">
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_need</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_raise</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_work</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_rec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_risk</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_esc</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_ins2</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_rel</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_close</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_46_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_46_start" name="Excavation or work has disturbed a surface"><messageEventDefinition id="n_46_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_46_ass" name="Assess the surface and public exposure"><documentation>4.6.1.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_46_tmp" name="Place and secure the temporary restoration"><documentation>4.6.1. With location, condition and the inspection need recorded - 4.6.2 has nothing to inspect against otherwise.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_46_need" name="Permanent restoration required"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_46_raise" name="Define the reinstatement obligation and its deadline"><documentation>4.6.3. The permit or jurisdiction deadline is recorded here, and 4.6.6 tracks against it.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_46_work" name="Create and route the restoration work"><documentation>4.6.3. Linked to the originating field work, so the obligation survives the work order that created it.</documentation></sendTask>
    <startEvent id="n_46_t" name="Temporary-condition inspection due"><timerEventDefinition id="n_46_t_td"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_46_insp" name="Inspect surface, barriers and public exposure"><documentation>4.6.2.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_46_acc" name="Condition acceptable"/>
    <userTask id="n_46_fix" name="Repair or renew the temporary restoration"><documentation>4.6.2.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_46_rec" name="Record the inspection and the next action"><documentation>4.6.2.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_46_risk" name="Permanent work at risk"/>
    <sendTask id="n_46_esc" name="Escalate to the obligation owner"><documentation>4.6.2 and 4.6.6.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_46_perm" name="Prepare the surface and place the permanent material"><documentation>4.6.4. With traffic and public protection applied under the MUTCD.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_46_evid" name="Record the completed condition and evidence"><documentation>4.6.4.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_46_ins2" name="Request jurisdiction inspection with the evidence"><documentation>4.6.5.</documentation></sendTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_46_rel" name="Accepted"/>
    <userTask id="n_46_corr" name="Correct the rejected condition"><documentation>4.6.5.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_46_close" name="Close tracking on accepted release"><documentation>4.6.6. Closed on the release, not on the paving.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_46_end" name="Site restored and released"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_start_n_46_ass" sourceRef="n_46_start" targetRef="n_46_ass" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_ass_n_46_tmp" sourceRef="n_46_ass" targetRef="n_46_tmp" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_tmp_n_46_need" sourceRef="n_46_tmp" targetRef="n_46_need" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_need_n_46_raise" sourceRef="n_46_need" targetRef="n_46_raise" name="permanent required"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_need_n_46_close" sourceRef="n_46_need" targetRef="n_46_close" name="temporary is the final surface"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_raise_n_46_work" sourceRef="n_46_raise" targetRef="n_46_work" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_work_n_46_perm" sourceRef="n_46_work" targetRef="n_46_perm" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_t_n_46_insp" sourceRef="n_46_t" targetRef="n_46_insp" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_insp_n_46_acc" sourceRef="n_46_insp" targetRef="n_46_acc" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_acc_n_46_fix" sourceRef="n_46_acc" targetRef="n_46_fix" name="not acceptable"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[acceptable = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_fix_n_46_rec" sourceRef="n_46_fix" targetRef="n_46_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_acc_n_46_rec" sourceRef="n_46_acc" targetRef="n_46_rec" name="acceptable"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_rec_n_46_risk" sourceRef="n_46_rec" targetRef="n_46_risk" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_risk_n_46_esc" sourceRef="n_46_risk" targetRef="n_46_esc" name="deadline at risk"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[atRisk = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_risk_n_46_t" sourceRef="n_46_risk" targetRef="n_46_t" name="on track"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_esc_n_46_perm" sourceRef="n_46_esc" targetRef="n_46_perm" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_perm_n_46_evid" sourceRef="n_46_perm" targetRef="n_46_evid" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_evid_n_46_ins2" sourceRef="n_46_evid" targetRef="n_46_ins2" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_ins2_n_46_rel" sourceRef="n_46_ins2" targetRef="n_46_rel" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_rel_n_46_corr" sourceRef="n_46_rel" targetRef="n_46_corr" name="rejected"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[accepted = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_corr_n_46_ins2" sourceRef="n_46_corr" targetRef="n_46_ins2" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_rel_n_46_close" sourceRef="n_46_rel" targetRef="n_46_close" name="accepted"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_46_close_n_46_end" sourceRef="n_46_close" targetRef="n_46_end" name=""/>
  </process>
